    "created_at": "2022-06-23T19:49:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-06-23T19:49:24Z",
    "body": "Oh right, it would bubble to the `ShadowRoot`. The composed flag is what causes the event to also bubble from `ShadowRoot` to its host and onward up.\r\n\r\nBut why does `ShadowRoot` have an `onslotchange` event handler attribute specifically, and not one for every event that might bubble up to it?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/dom/issues/comments/1164805733/reactions",
